            "script": "// Busy intervals per user per date (minutes from 00:00)\n// Working day: 9:00-17:00 = 540-1020 minutes\n// Starts: 540, 570, ..., 960 (16:00)\n\nto_min = fun(t) {\n  parts = text.split(t, \":\")\n  return number.parse(parts[0]) * 60 + number.parse(parts[1])\n}\n\nusers_data = json.parse(input)\n// Build busy as list of {start,end} in minutes for each date across all users (union)\n\ndates = [\"2026-06-15\", \"2026-06-16\", \"2026-06-17\", \"2026-06-18\", \"2026-06-19\"]\n\n// For each date, collect all busy intervals from all users\n// Then find earliest start s in [540,570,...,960] such that [s,s+60] overlaps no busy\n\nstarts = for i in list.range(0, 15) {  // 0..14 -> 540 + i*30\n  return 540 + i * 30\n}\n\nresult = fold acc = null for d in dates {\n  skip if acc != null\n  // union of busy\n  all_busy = fold bacc = [] for u in users_data.users {\n    day = fold found = null for day in u.days {\n      skip if day.date != d\n      return day\n    }\n    busy_list = day.busy if day != null else []\n    intervals = for b in busy_list {\n      return { start: to_min(b.start), end: to_min(b.end) }\n    }\n    return bacc + intervals\n  }\n  // check each start\n  chosen = fold c = null for s in starts {\n    skip if c != null\n    e = s + 60\n    // overlaps any busy?\n    conflict = fold hit = false for b in all_busy {\n      skip if hit\n      // overlap if s < b.end and e > b.start\n      ov = s < b.end and e > b.start\n      return ov\n    }\n    return { start_min: s, end_min: e, date: d } if not conflict\n  }\n  return chosen\n}\n\nassert(result != null, \"no slot found\")\n\n// format ISO\nhm = fun(m) {\n  h = number.floor(m / 60)\n  mi = m - h * 60\n  hs = text.slice(\"0\" + json.encode(h), -2, null)\n  ms = text.slice(\"0\" + json.encode(mi), -2, null)\n  return hs + \":\" + ms + \":00\"\n}\n\nstart_iso = result.date + \"T\" + hm(result.start_min) + \"Z\"\nend_iso = result.date + \"T\" + hm(result.end_min) + \"Z\"\n\nsub = submit_result({ answer: { start: start_iso, end: end_iso } })\nreturn { start: start_iso, end: end_iso, recorded: sub.recorded }"
